4. Assess demand vs channel-stuffing: For each of the top-3 anomalies, compute supporting signals from the CSV: (a) return rate in the anomaly month vs the 24-month average return rate for that combo, (b) whether the following 1-2 months show a sharp drop (reversal), (c) whether the spike is isolated or part of a trend. Save a signals CSV → code_agent
5. Write Markdown report: Write a comprehensive Markdown report to disk (e.g. offline_data/regional_sales_anomaly_report.md). Requirements: H1 title, at least one data table, every key number annotated with source in the format '（来源：offline_data/regional_sales.csv 的 <列名>，<聚合口径与样本行数>）' or '（来源：由前述两行计算）', and a concluding paragraph judging whether each spike is real demand or channel stuffing. All conclusions must derive solely from the local CSV. → code_agent
